  "detailed_description": "The Anti-Bird Net Scheme, an initiative by the Agriculture Department of the Rajasthan government, promotes protected cultivation practices among farmers by providing subsidies for installing low-cost plastic tunnels. The subsidy amount may be capped for each farmer, depending on the scheme&#39;s provisions and available funds.\n> **Important points**\n\n\n1. The work can be started only after the administrative approval/work order is issued by the Horticulture Department.\n1. After establishment, verification can be done by the committee formed.\n1. The grant amount can be paid directly into the farmer&#39;s bank account or to the producing firm based on the written consent of the farmer.\n\n<br>\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n1. The applicant should be a native of Rajasthan.\n1. The applicant must have ownership of cultivable land, his own fruit orchard, and an irrigation source.\n\n",
  "exclusions": null,
